window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Quick Start","u":"getting-started.html#quick-start","x":""},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"See it working (1 minute)","u":"getting-started.html#see-it-working-1-minute","x":"Choose Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Open Demo > Menu Tour (uGUI) . Press Play . The screen dims, the Play button is spotlighted and a tip card explains it. Click Play in the game: the step finishes and the tour moves on. On the last step but one, click Make it yours to switch between the five built-in looks."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Your own tutorial (5 minutes)","u":"getting-started.html#your-own-tutorial-5-minutes","x":"Open your scene. Select the buttons or objects the tutorial should point at, in the order the player meets them. Choose Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Add Selected As Steps . You get a Tutorial Flow with one step per object. Steps that point at a button already wait for a click on it. Select a step and write its heading and text in the Inspector. With Live Preview on (the default), the Game view shows the step without pressing Play. Press Play ."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"What next","u":"getting-started.html#what-next","x":"Change how each step finishes: add a rule such as Key Rule or Area Rule to the step ( Finishing a Step ). For an action game, set the flow's Style to Hint : small tips that never block or pause play ( Coach Marks and Hints ). Pick a look under Theme Preset , or make your own theme ( Make It Yours ). If something doesn't happen, open Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Why Is This Step Waiting ."},{"p":"Samples","h":"Samples","u":"samples.html#samples","x":"Open each from Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Open Demo and press Play. Demo Shows Menu Tour (uGUI) A mobile-style menu, a coach-mark tour with spotlights, a click on the real Play button, and a Make it yours button that switches the five looks. First Person Basics (3D hints) In-game hints that never pause play: walk (W A S D), look at the tower, jump, reach the glowing pad, collect 3 coins. Button pictures follow your device. Platformer Hints (2D) Hints on 2D colliders with an orthographic camera: run, jump onto the ledge, coins, reach the flag. Strategy Tour (UI Toolkit) A coach-mark tour"},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"Flows and Steps","u":"flows-and-steps.html#flows-and-steps","x":"A Tutorial Flow is one tutorial. Its steps are its child objects with a Tutorial Step component, shown in order from top to bottom. Reorder steps by reordering the children, or with the arrows in the flow's Inspector."},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"The flow","u":"flows-and-steps.html#the-flow","x":"Setting What it does Theme Preset / Theme The look (see Make It Yours ). Style Coach Mark dims and waits; Hint is small and never blocks. Steps can override it. Input Gate What the player can click: only the target, only the card, or everything. Steps can override it. Start On Scene Start , or Manually (a trigger, a button, a UnityEvent or code calls Play). Run Once Per Player Once the player finishes or skips it, it never runs again for them (on this install, or in this save slot with a profile: see Progress). Resume Where Left If the player quits halfway, the flow continues from the same ste"},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"The step","u":"flows-and-steps.html#the-step","x":"Setting What it does Title, Text The tip card's words. Short sentences work best. Short Text A few words for compact cards and hints. Icon A picture shown when the look's Display As uses icons. Glyph Action Shows the button picture for this action on the player's device (Jump, Interact...). Target What the step points at (see Targets ). When Target Missing Wait for it (default: nothing shows or blocks until it appears), show the card anyway, or skip the step. Finish When Any rule or all rules. A step with no rule finishes with Next. Next Button Auto shows it when the step has no rule. Optional"},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"Starting a flow","u":"flows-and-steps.html#starting-a-flow","x":"On Scene Start : it plays as soon as the scene starts. Tutorial Trigger component: when the player enters an area (3D or 2D trigger), the first time an object is seen on screen, when an object turns on, or after a delay. Play from a UnityEvent (a button's On Click) or from code: flow.Play() ."},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"Progress","u":"flows-and-steps.html#progress","x":"Progress is saved in PlayerPrefs under RomanoAssets.TutorialKit.<flow id> . PlayerPrefs belong to this install of the game: for save slots or several players call TutorialProgress.UseProfile(\"slot-2\") , or keep progress with your game's saves by setting TutorialProgress.Store to your own ITutorialProgressStore (see Extending ). TutorialProgress.ClearAll() forgets everything (a new game, or \"Reset tutorials\" in your options). Restart starts one flow again from its first step. Each step saves a stable key next to its position, so inserting, moving or removing steps in an update never resumes a p"},{"p":"Flows and Steps","h":"Pausing","u":"flows-and-steps.html#pausing","x":"Tutorials run on real time, so they keep working while your game is paused ( Time.timeScale = 0 ): good for menu tours. When your pause menu, a dialogue or a loading screen opens over a running tutorial, call flow.Suspend() (or TutorialFlow.SuspendAll(true) ) and Resume() when it closes: nothing shows or blocks meanwhile, and its rules and timers wait."},{"p":"Targets","h":"Targets","u":"targets.html#targets","x":"Each step points at one target. The spotlight, outline and pointer follow it every frame, so moving and animated targets are fine. Kind Set Notes None nothing A plain message in the middle of the screen. UI Element a uGUI RectTransform (button, icon, panel) Any canvas mode; clicks on it can finish the step. UI Toolkit Element a UI Document and an element name (or a USS class) Names as set in UI Builder. World Object any object Uses its renderers (3D meshes, sprites), else its 3D or 2D colliders, else its position. Screen Area a rectangle as fractions of the screen 0,0 is bottom left, 1,1 is to"},{"p":"Targets","h":"Spawned, pooled and list items: Found By Id","u":"targets.html#spawned-pooled-and-list-items-found-by-id","x":"Menus built from prefabs, inventory slots, pooled UI and objects in other scenes can't be dragged into a step. Instead: Add Add Component > All In One Tutorial Kit > Tutorial Target Id to the object or prefab, and type an id ( inventory.sword ). Set the step's target to Found By Id with the same id. The step waits until an active object with that id exists, then highlights it (a uGUI element like UI Element, anything else like World Object). If the object is turned off or returned to a pool, the step hides and waits again; the newest active object with the id wins. Use a different id for each "},{"p":"Targets","h":"Clicks","u":"targets.html#clicks","x":"On a button (or any Selectable), only a click the button really takes counts: a click on a button that isn't interactable doesn't finish the step. Gamepad and keyboard Submit on the highlighted button counts too, and gamepad players get the highlighted button selected. On a plain panel or picture, a press and release inside it counts."},{"p":"Targets","h":"Lists: Scroll Into View","u":"targets.html#lists-scroll-into-view","x":"A uGUI target inside a Scroll Rect (a shop list, an inventory) is scrolled into view when its step starts, so the spotlight never points at an item the list's mask hides. Turn Scroll Into View off on the target to leave the list alone."},{"p":"Targets","h":"World objects","u":"targets.html#world-objects","x":"Bounds chooses what the highlight wraps: Auto, Renderers, Colliders, or Position (with a size you set). Camera : the camera that sees it. Empty uses the main camera, or the first camera that sees the object. For split screen, set the player's camera here. Cameras that render into a Render Texture aren't supported. When the object is behind the camera or outside the view, the pointer sits at the screen edge and points toward it."},{"p":"Targets","h":"When a target can't be found","u":"targets.html#when-a-target-cant-be-found","x":"When Target Missing on the step decides (the menu is closed, the object isn't spawned yet, it was turned off): Choice What happens Wait (default) Nothing shows and nothing is blocked until the target appears, then the step shows. The game can never get stuck behind a dim screen. Show Card The card shows in the middle of the screen without a highlight. Skip Step The step is passed over. Why Is This Step Waiting and Scene Overview say what is wrong: not set, turned off, not under a Canvas, no element with that name, no object with that id yet, or no camera."},{"p":"Finishing a Step","h":"Finishing a Step","u":"finishing-steps.html#finishing-a-step","x":"Add one or more rules to a step's object (Add Component > All In One Tutorial Kit > Rules). The step finishes when any rule is done, or when all are (the step's Finish When ). A step with no rule finishes with the Next button. Every rule runs on real time and tells the debugger what it is waiting for. Rule Finishes when Notes Click Target Rule the player clicks or taps the step's target uGUI, UI Toolkit, world objects and screen areas. Set how many clicks. Key Rule one of its keys is pressed (or held for a time) Both input systems. Input Action Rule an Input System action is performed Gamepads"},{"p":"Finishing a Step","h":"Tips","u":"finishing-steps.html#tips","x":"\"Press Space or tap Jump\": add a Key Rule and a Click Target Rule, Finish When Any Rule. \"Collect 3 coins\": a Counter Rule, and each coin's pickup event calls the rule's Add . \"If the player already knows this, skip it\": tick the step's Skip If Already Done . A Condition Rule or a Counter Rule with Count Before Step Starts is done straight away when the player already did it. Your own rule: derive from CompletionRule (see Extending )."},{"p":"Coach Marks and Hints","h":"Coach Marks and Hints","u":"coach-marks-and-hints.html#coach-marks-and-hints","x":"Every step shows in one of two styles. Set it on the flow ( Style ) and override it per step."},{"p":"Coach Marks and Hints","h":"Coach marks","u":"coach-marks-and-hints.html#coach-marks","x":"For menus, mobile games and strategy games. The screen dims around a spotlight on the target, a pointer shows the way, and the tip card waits beside it. The Input Gate decides what the player can click: Only Target : the target (and the card) only. Clicks inside the spotlight reach the real button. Block All : only the card's buttons. Allow All : nothing is blocked."},{"p":"Coach Marks and Hints","h":"In-game hints","u":"coach-marks-and-hints.html#in-game-hints","x":"For action games. A small tip that never dims, never blocks and never pauses play: \"Press Space to jump\", gone when the player jumps. Hints fit their words, sit at the bottom, top or centre of the screen (or beside their target), and can still ring their target. Set where they appear under the theme's In-game hints settings. Use Show Until Learned on the flow for hints that come back until the player has done the thing a few times, and a Tutorial Trigger to show a hint the first time the player meets something."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Make It Yours","u":"make-it-yours.html#make-it-yours","x":"Everything the player sees and hears can be changed or switched off, without code."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Looks","u":"make-it-yours.html#looks","x":"Pick a Theme Preset on the flow: Clean Dark , Minimal , Mobile Casual , Sci-Fi HUD or Fantasy Parchment . For your own, choose Assets > Create > All In One Tutorial Kit > Theme , set it on the flow's Theme field and change anything. Presets keep your own pictures, font and sounds when you switch. Group Settings Overlay Dim on or off, colour and strength. Spotlight Shape (rounded rectangle, circle, oval, none), padding, corner radius, softness. Outline On or off, colour, width, pulse. Pointer On or off, colour, size, bob, your own picture. Message Display As, card position, custom point and off"},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Display As","u":"make-it-yours.html#display-as","x":"How much each card shows: Full (heading and text), Short Text , Icon Only , Icon And Short Text , or None (only the highlight; buttons still show when the step needs Next). Set it on the theme, override it per step."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Card position","u":"make-it-yours.html#card-position","x":"Auto picks the side with room; or Below , Above , Right , Left , Center , Screen Top , Screen Bottom , or Custom (a point on screen plus an offset). The card never leaves the screen or covers its target."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Per step","u":"make-it-yours.html#per-step","x":"Any step can have its own look ( Theme Override ), Display As, position, style and input gate."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Your own pictures","u":"make-it-yours.html#your-own-pictures","x":"Card, main button and pointer each take your sprite. Sprites with borders are 9-sliced; all are tinted by the part's colour."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Words","u":"make-it-yours.html#words","x":"Every word goes through TutorialText.Translate : set it to your localisation lookup, and you can write keys instead of sentences in steps."},{"p":"Make It Yours","h":"Accessibility","u":"make-it-yours.html#accessibility","x":"UI Scale on the presenter for larger text, Reduce Motion on the theme, high-contrast looks (Minimal), and real time timers that you can lengthen."},{"p":"Button Pictures","h":"Button Pictures","u":"button-pictures.html#button-pictures","x":"Set a step's Glyph Action (for example Jump) and its card shows the right picture for the player's device: Space on a keyboard, A on Xbox, Cross on PlayStation, B on Nintendo Switch, a swipe on a touch screen. It switches live when the player picks up another device, with either input system. The kit's set ( Default Input Glyphs , made from Kenney's Input Prompts, CC0) has these actions: Confirm, Back, Jump, Interact, Attack, Aim, Move, Look, Menu, Tap, Hold, Swipe, Pinch."},{"p":"Button Pictures","h":"Your own set","u":"button-pictures.html#your-own-set","x":"Choose Assets > Create > All In One Tutorial Kit > Input Glyph Set , add your actions and pictures, and set it on the flow's Glyphs field. A device with no picture falls back to the keyboard picture. On light cards, the theme's Icon Plate Color puts a plate behind white button pictures so they stay readable."},{"p":"Button Pictures","h":"Words that fit every device","u":"button-pictures.html#words-that-fit-every-device","x":"The picture changes with the player's device; the words don't. Write the action, not the key (\"Jump onto the ledge\", not \"Press Space to jump onto the ledge\"), and let the button picture show which button to press. For per-device words, translate them through TutorialText.Translate and call TutorialFlow.RefreshAllViews() when the device changes."},{"p":"Tools","h":"Tools","u":"tools.html#tools","x":"Everything is under Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit . Tool What it does Create Tutorial Flow A new flow with one step. Create From Preset Menu Tour (coach marks), Movement Basics (in-game hints), First Time Hint (shown the first time something is seen). Add Selected As Steps Select buttons or objects, get one step per object with its target set; steps on buttons wait for a click. Picking a button's label or icon points at the button itself. Add Step Ready-made steps: Explain Something (Next button), Click A Button (select it first), Press A Key (in-game hint), Walk Somewhere (in-game hint), Wa"},{"p":"Tools","h":"In the Inspector","u":"tools.html#in-the-inspector","x":"The Tutorial Flow Inspector lists the steps in order with Edit and move buttons, Add Step, and Restart, Next and Skip while playing. At the top of the Tutorial Step Inspector, a box says in plain words when the step finishes (\"a click on Play Button, or the Next button\") and what it points at, lists anything wrong with it (with a fix button), and while playing has Test From This Step and what the step is waiting for right now."},{"p":"Tools","h":"In the Scene view","u":"tools.html#in-the-scene-view","x":"Select a flow or a step to see a box and the step number on each world target."},{"p":"Tools","h":"In your game","u":"tools.html#in-your-game","x":"Add a Tutorial Debug Overlay to any object and press F8 in a test build to see what each running flow waits for, with a box around each target."},{"p":"Integrations","h":"Integrations","u":"integrations.html#integrations","x":"The kit needs no package. These work automatically when their package or kit is in your project. With What you get uGUI (in every Unity template) The kit's tip card, spotlight and input gate for uGUI. UI Toolkit (built into Unity) UI Toolkit targets, and a UI Toolkit tip card. It is used when uGUI isn't in the project; add UI Toolkit Tutorial Presenter to a flow to use it anyway. Input System package Keys, pointer, touch, gamepad detection and the Input Action Rule . With Input Handling set to Both, the Input System is used. Visual Scripting package Visual Scripting Event Rule : a graph's Cust"},{"p":"Integrations","h":"Saving progress with your save system","u":"integrations.html#saving-progress-with-your-save-system","x":"Progress goes to PlayerPrefs by default. To keep it in your own saves, implement ITutorialProgressStore (five small methods: get and set the step, get and set done, clear) and set it once at start: TutorialProgress.Store = new MySaveSystemProgressStore();"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Extending","u":"extending.html#extending","x":"Everything works without code. For programmers, the kit is built to be extended."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Control a flow","u":"extending.html#control-a-flow","x":"flow.Play(); // start (respects Run Once and Resume) flow.Next(); // finish the current step flow.Back(); flow.Skip(); // end it and remember it as done flow.Restart(); // start again from the first step flow.Stop(); // stop without saving it as done (it resumes next time) flow.Suspend(); // hold it: nothing shows or blocks, rules and timers wait flow.Resume(); // show the held step again flow.RefreshView(); // redraw after changing the look or words at runtime flow.ClearProgress(); // forget this player's progress for this flow Read IsRunning , IsSuspended , CurrentIndex , CurrentStep , StepV"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Find and start flows from anywhere","u":"extending.html#find-and-start-flows-from-anywhere","x":"TutorialFlow.PlayById(\"shop-tour\"); // from a button in another scene, a quest, a dialogue... TutorialFlow.Find(\"shop-tour\"); // the loaded flow with that id, or null TutorialFlow.SuspendAll(true); // your pause menu or loading screen opened TutorialFlow.SuspendAll(false); // and closed TutorialFlow.RefreshAllViews(); // the player changed the language A flow lives in its scene. For a tutorial that goes from the menu into the level, make one flow in each scene and start the second with PlayById (or Start: On Scene Start ) after the level loads. Only one coach-mark flow shows at a time: a secon"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Events and analytics","u":"extending.html#events-and-analytics","x":"Each flow has Started , StepShown , Completed , Skipped (C#) and the matching UnityEvents. For analytics, listen to every flow at once: TutorialFlow.AnyEvent += e => MyAnalytics.Log(\"tutorial\", e.Kind.ToString(), e.FlowId, e.StepKey, e.ElapsedSeconds); The kinds are FlowStarted, StepShown, StepCompleted, FlowCompleted, FlowSkipped, FlowStopped, FlowSuspended and FlowResumed. Every flow ends with exactly one of Completed, Skipped or Stopped. StepKey stays the same when you move or insert steps, so your funnels keep working after updates. The kit itself sends nothing anywhere."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Progress, save slots and profiles","u":"extending.html#progress-save-slots-and-profiles","x":"Progress is saved in PlayerPrefs, which belong to this install of the game. For save slots or several players: TutorialProgress.UseProfile(\"slot-2\"); // when the player picks a slot, before tutorials start TutorialProgress.ClearAll(); // \"Reset tutorials\" in your options, or a new game Or keep progress in your own save file: implement ITutorialProgressStore (five methods) and set TutorialProgress.Store . Each step saves a stable key with its position, so adding, moving or removing steps in an update never resumes a player at the wrong step (an unknown saved step starts the flow from the beginn"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Targets that appear later","u":"extending.html#targets-that-appear-later","x":"TutorialTargets.Register(\"shop.buy\", buyButton.transform); TutorialTargets.Unregister(\"shop.buy\", buyButton.transform); Or put a Tutorial Target Id component on the prefab. See Targets."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Your own rule","u":"extending.html#your-own-rule","x":"public sealed class OpenedMapRule : CompletionRule { protected override void OnBegin() => MapScreen.Opened += Done; protected override void OnEnd() => MapScreen.Opened -= Done; private void Done() => MarkDone(); public override void DescribeWaiting(System.Text.StringBuilder into) => into.Append(\"the map to open\"); } Add it to a step like any rule. OnTick runs every frame (real time) while the step shows; OnTargetClicked runs when the player clicks the target. Unsubscribe in OnEnd : it always runs once when the step ends, is skipped or the flow's object is destroyed."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Your own UI","u":"extending.html#your-own-ui","x":"Implement ITutorialPresenter on a component and put it on the flow's object (or drag it into Presenter ). The flow calls ShowStep with everything already resolved (words, look, buttons, icon, position), UpdateTarget every frame with the target's screen rectangle, then HideStep and EndFlow . Call flow.Next() , Back() , Skip() and NotifyTargetClicked() from your buttons. If your UI reports clicks on uGUI targets itself, set flow.TargetReportsClicks = true ; otherwise the flow counts a press inside the target. To make your UI the default for every flow, set TutorialPresenters.CreateDefault ."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Your own input","u":"extending.html#your-own-input","x":"Implement ITutorialInputSource and set TutorialInput.Source to drive tutorials from any input system (Rewired, InControl, your own) or a replay. If players can type somewhere the kit doesn't know about, add a check so typed letters aren't counted as key presses: TutorialInput.AddTypingCheck(() => myChatBox.IsTyping) ."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Words","u":"extending.html#words","x":"TutorialText.Translate = key => MyLocalisation.Get(key); and call TutorialFlow.RefreshAllViews() when the language changes."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Condition Rule and IL2CPP","u":"extending.html#condition-rule-and-il2cpp","x":"The Condition Rule reads a field or property by name. With IL2CPP and high code stripping, a member only read this way can be removed: mark it [UnityEngine.Scripting.Preserve] , or use an Event Rule for anything the tutorial depends on."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Upgrading","u":"upgrading.html#upgrading","x":"Updates never change your flows, steps or themes. Import the new version over the old one; your progress keys ( RomanoAssets.TutorialKit.<flow id> ) stay the same. What changed in each version is in CHANGELOG.md ."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Troubleshooting","u":"troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","x":"First open Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Why Is This Step Waiting while playing, and Scene Overview in the editor: they say what is wrong in plain words, and Scene Overview fixes most of it in one click. The tutorial doesn't start. It may have run before: with Run Once Per Player on, a finished or skipped flow never runs again for that player. Press Restart in the flow's Inspector while playing. Or its Start is Manually: something has to call Play (a Tutorial Trigger, a button, a UnityEvent). A step never finishes. The debugger says what it waits for (the step's Inspector says it too). A s"},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Still stuck?","u":"troubleshooting.html#still-stuck","x":"Discord: https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu (ask in #help) Report a bug: https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport/issues Website: https://raregeometry.github.io/tutorial-kit/ Press Copy system info in Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Help and Support and paste it into your message."},{"p":"Support","h":"Support","u":"support.html#support","x":""},{"p":"Support","h":"Where to get help","u":"support.html#where-to-get-help","x":"Documentation: https://raregeometry.github.io/tutorial-kit/docs/ Discord: https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu Ask in #help , report problems in #bug-reports , suggest ideas in #feature-requests , with the Tutorial Kit tag. Report a bug: https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport/issues Search the open issues first, then use the Bug report form and pick this kit. Website: https://raregeometry.github.io/tutorial-kit/ Email: raregeometrysupport@gmail.com"},{"p":"Support","h":"What to include","u":"support.html#what-to-include","x":"Open Tools > All In One Tutorial Kit > Help and Support and press Copy system info : it copies the kit version, Unity version, render pipeline, platform and input handling. Paste it into your post, then add what you did, what you expected, what happened, and any Console errors."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#changelog","x":"All notable changes to the All In One Tutorial Kit are listed here, newest first, in the Keep a Changelog style."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"[1.0.0] - 2026-11-08","u":"changelog.html#100---2026-11-08","x":""},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Added","u":"changelog.html#added","x":"First release. Tip card placement that keeps the card on screen and off its target, Help and Support window. Tutorial Flow with steps as child objects, Next, Back, Skip, Restart, run once per player and resume, on real time so it works while the game is paused. Progress in PlayerPrefs or your own store. Targets: uGUI elements, UI Toolkit elements, 2D and 3D world objects (renderers, colliders or position, any camera), screen areas, or none. Off-screen world targets get an edge marker. Completion rules: Click Target, Timer and Event, combined as any or all. uGUI presenter: dim overlay with a cr"}];
